{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018neMKDsDcyPeXMJBDJuCBE","type":"tool_result","content":"33:  (default 1920×1080), `-o`, `--fps`, `--durationMs`, `--props`, `--save-mosaic`,\n54:| `hello-world` | The first render — a thin alias for `make @m0saic/hello-world/v1` (the brand card; output defaults to `hello-world.mp4`). With `--template-repo <path...>` / `--community-repo <path>` it renders the loaded repo's **front door** instead: the first repo (load order) whose `repo.helloWorld` names a template that registered, announced as `Front door: <id> — <repo>'s hello-world`; no repos, or none that name one → the core card with a one-line why. Takes `-o -w -h --fps --durationMs --props --quiet --verbose` (no engine surface). Picker: the CLI source (not published). |\n102:   `--props` over `defaultProps`, render.\n162:`--alpha`/`--no-alpha`, `--props <jsonOrPath>` (inline JSON **or** `@path/to/json`\n350:macOS; `--app <path>` override); `open --template <id> [--props/--props-file]`\nUsage: m0saic make [options] <input>\n\nRender a template id (built-in, or from a loaded repo) or a .mosaic / .mosaicx\nfile to video or image. The template (or the file) decides whether the result\nis a video or an image; -o's extension must agree.\n\nArguments:\n  input                            A template id (e.g. @m0saic/…/v1 — m0saic\n                                   list-templates), a .mosaic document, or a\n                                   .mosaicx recipe\n\nOptions:\n  -w, --width <num>                Output width in pixels (default: the file's\n                                   own size / the template's authored canvas)\n  -h, --height <num>               Output height in pixels (default: the file's\n                                   own size / the template's authored canvas)\n  --fps <num>                      Override output frames-per-second (1–120)\n  --durationMs <num>               Override output duration in milliseconds (>\n                                   0)\n  -o, --output <file>              Output file path. Its extension must match\n                                   the template's kind (video → .mp4 / .webm /\n                                   .mov, image → .png / .jpg). Default: the\n                                   template's own name, else out.mp4 / out.png\n                                   — --validate-only without -o prints which\n  --props <jsonOrPath>             Template props as JSON or @path/to/json\n  --tutorial                       Render the template's self-documenting\n                                   TUTORIAL (its renderTutorial path) instead\n                                   of the normal output. Tutorials always use\n                                   the template's own defaultProps and their\n                                   own step timing; --props/--inputs/--duration\n                                   are ignored. Errors if the template declares\n                                   no tutorial. Template-id input only.\n  --inputs <files...>              Multiple source files for templates that\n                                   accept `sourceIds: string[]` (e.g.\n                                   screencap_grid). Repeatable list; populates\n                                   `sourceIds` on the props. Wins over\n                                   --input-dir on conflict.\n  --input-dir <path>               Folder of source media for templates that\n                                   accept `sourceIds`. The media kind follows\n                                   the template's own input declaration (videos\n                                   for screencap grids, images for the image\n                                   collage); expands to a deterministic\n                                   alphabetical list. Same effect as --inputs\n                                   but ergonomic for batch flows.\n  --recursive                      With --input-dir: also walk subfolders\n                                   (deterministic depth-first order).\n  --output-kind <kind>             Override the output kind (video | image).\n                                   Off by default — the template decides.\n                                   --output-kind video -o out.mp4 renders an\n                                   image template as a clip held for its\n                                   duration; the other way round (an animated\n                                   template as one image) is not supported\n  --format <kind>                  Same as --output-kind (older spelling;\n                                   --output-kind wins when both are given)\n  --alpha                          Request alpha output (where supported)\n  --no-alpha                       Disable alpha output\n\nTemplate repos (local folders — m0saic --help explains the two flags):\n  --template-repo <path...>        Load a template repo from a local folder — a\n                                   starter clone, your own (repeatable).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fadc3ba2-c902-457a-8c6b-b57eed4efb97","uuid":"7583eea2-8787-4dbd-8074-96fe36e219ce","timestamp":"2026-09-29T14:50:54.166Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"33:  (default 1920×1080), `-o`, `--fps`, `--durationMs`, `--props`, `--save-mosaic`,\n54:| `hello-world` | The first render — a thin alias for `make @m0saic/hello-world/v1` (the brand card; output defaults to `hello-world.mp4`). With `--template-repo <path...>` / `--community-repo <path>` it renders the loaded repo's **front door** instead: the first repo (load order) whose `repo.helloWorld` names a template that registered, announced as `Front door: <id> — <repo>'s hello-world`; no repos, or none that name one → the core card with a one-line why. Takes `-o -w -h --fps --durationMs --props --quiet --verbose` (no engine surface). Picker: the CLI source (not published). |\n102:   `--props` over `defaultProps`, render.\n