{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011rDyDQSwKLKNx6vfXSqGWM","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-09-29\\30-build.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fadc3ba2-c902-457a-8c6b-b57eed4efb97","uuid":"f2b20db2-7499-46e8-83ef-0d06a1c2caa2","timestamp":"2026-09-29T14:55:56.545Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-09-29\\30-build.md","oldString":"- Cost probe (`scratch/cost-probe.cjs`): 25x25 at 1080x1080 is 86 frames,\n  86 sources, overlay depth 13-14 (budget 20), 4 inline masks. Now asserted\n  in the test.\n- Next: re-render variant a, stress renders 15x15 / 21x21, variants b and c.","newString":"- The 21x21 stress render warned `OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP` (a root overlay chain\n  37 deep, threshold 20, \"past ~25 nested overlays ffmpeg SILENTLY degrades\n  inline masks\"): call 1 drew letters and numbers as one text source PER ROW.\n  Now one source holds every letter and one every number. 25x25 went from 86\n  to 38 sources, the warning is gone, the 21x21 renders in 2.0 s (was 6.4 s),\n  and the picture is unchanged. Asserted in the test.\n- Stress renders in `stress/` (15x15, 21x21, a 15x15 teaser at 1080x1080,\n  both grids at 480x270): exit 0, no engine warnings.\n- Next: variant a re-rendered with the final code, then b and c.","originalFile":"# Build — 2026-09-29\n\n(in progress - call 4, the resumed build)\n\n## Template: @one-a-day/gaming/crossword-grid-card/v1\n\nConstruction decision (call 1): the brief asked for Recipe 3 (a `grid()` with\nindex-aligned overlay grids for fills, letters and numbers). The gate's\n`costBudget` caps a render at 400 frames and 400 sources\n(`COST_BUDGETS` in `@m0saic/template-utils`), and a 15x15 as per-cell grids is\n225 fills + ~190 letters + ~70 numbers. So the board is drawn instead as:\n\n- paper: one tile under the board;\n- theme: one tile masked (inline-mask) to the theme cells;\n- ink: one tile masked to \"board minus paper cells\", which gives the border,\n  the rules and the blocks in one path;\n- rings: one tile masked to the circled cells' annuli;\n- letters and numbers: one multi-layer svg text source per row, each layer\n  placed by a pixel `xExpr`/`yExpr` (probe render in `scratch/probe/`).\n\nEvery rect goes through `placeInsetPieces`; the cell lattice is authored as\ninteger lines `X_k = round(x0 + k*pitch)`, so cells are equal within 1 px and\nno split count depends on the grid size (13, 17, 19, 23 need no `lattice.allow`).\n\n## Call 4 (resume) so far\n\n- m0saic 0.3.0 doctor `bindingsDeclared` fixed by binding, not declaring:\n  the board ink tile carries `bindProps` [grid, themeEntries, circles,\n  themeColor] (grid first = the double-click; the teaser board offers only\n  grid and circles); each theme-list id cell binds ITS token of the raw\n  `themeEntries` string (`bindPropRange` focus); the list swatches bind\n  `themeColor`; the caption line is split into three cells (publication,\n  date, the rest) so `date` has its own handle and the derived rest\n  (`| 7x7 | solution`) stays unbound.\n- `npm run build` clean; `m0saic doctor . --json`: this template meets 0.3.0,\n  0 errors, 0 warnings (`logs/doctor-call4-a.json`).\n- Cost probe (`scratch/cost-probe.cjs`): 25x25 at 1080x1080 is 86 frames,\n  86 sources, overlay depth 13-14 (budget 20), 4 inline masks. Now asserted\n  in the test.\n- Next: re-render variant a, stress renders 15x15 / 21x21, variants b and c.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":34,"oldLines":7,"newStart":34,"newLines":12,"lines":["   (`| 7x7 | solution`) stays unbound."," - `npm run build` clean; `m0saic doctor . --json`: this template meets 0.3.0,","   0 errors, 0 warnings (`logs/doctor-call4-a.json`).","-- Cost probe (`scratch/cost-probe.cjs`): 25x25 at 1080x1080 is 86 frames,","-  86 sources, overlay depth 13-14 (budget 20), 4 inline masks. Now asserted","-  in the test.","-- Next: re-render variant a, stress renders 15x15 / 21x21, variants b and c.","+- The 21x21 stress render warned `OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP` (a root overlay chain","+  37 deep, threshold 20, \"past ~25 nested overlays ffmpeg SILENTLY degrades","+  inline masks\"): call 1 drew letters and numbers as one text source PER ROW.","+  Now one source holds every letter and one every number. 25x25 went from 86","+  to 38 sources, the warning is gone, the 21x21 renders in 2.0 s (was 6.4 s),","+  and the picture is unchanged. Asserted in the test.","+- Stress renders in `stress/` (15x15, 21x21, a 15x15 teaser at 1080x1080,","+  both grids at 480x270): exit 0, no engine warnings.","+- Next: variant a re-rendered with the final code, then b and c."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
