{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VJhGrpxTW1MvL1Ui7G5huJ","type":"tool_result","content":"=== agent a1b5bc4b982673729\n- medium | At the 1080x1080 hint, a title longer than about 18 characters shrinks below 1/20 of the short side instead of wrapping, and can end up smaller than the byline and theme list\n  evidence: The brief (Panel copy): \"title: the puzzle title, the largest panel text; wraps to at most 2 lines, then shrinks.\" The size ladder: \"The panel title is at least 1/20 of the short side at the primary canvases.\" In square mode the title gets titleMax = panel.h - metaH - bylineH - 2*gap, which is about 67 px (crossword-grid-card.ts:598). That height never fits two lines at a usable size, so fit() shrinks the title on one line. layoutCrosswordCard at 1080x1080 (review/brief/probe3.cjs), against S/20 = 54: \"Turning Things Around\" (21 chars) -> 49px, 1 line; \"A Sunday-Size Stress Grid\" (25) -> 42px; \"Sunday Puzzle: Turning Around\" (29) -> 35px; the 40-char max -> 26px, 1 line. probe12.cjs: with the 40-char title, the title is 26px while byline = 30px and theme-0/theme-1 = 32px, so it is the smallest line in the caption. This is visible in review/brief/max-title-1080.png and titles-strip.png. The build's own rubric-3 render journal/2026-09-29/stress/21x21-1080.png also has a 42px title. The test only checks the 13-char default title (test.ts:215-219), and 30-build.md does not mention this limit. At 1920x1080 and 1080x1920 every title tested stays at 54px or more.\n  repro: cd C:/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day && node journal/2026-09-29/review/brief/probe3.cjs && node journal/2026-09-29/review/brief/probe12.cjs; view journal/2026-09-29/review/brief/max-title-1080.png\n  fix: Give the square-mode title a height budget that fits 2 lines at S/20 or more. Options: shrink the board toward the brief's 0.72 lower bound, or let the title span the full strip width above the byline/meta and theme columns. Add a test with a 25-40 char title at 1080x1080. If the promise can't be met, disclose it in 30-build.md.\n- medium | Teaser mode (solved:false) resizes the title and moves the byline in square mode, against \"Nothing else moves\"\n  evidence: The brief (Unsolved mode): \"letters, theme tints and the theme list are hidden ...; the meta line says puzzle. Nothing else moves.\" Square mode sets leftW = panel.w * (showThemes ? 0.54 : 1) (ts:591), and showThemes is false when solved is false. So the title column roughly doubles in width in the teaser. probe4.cjs, solved vs teaser at 1080x1080: title \"Turning Things Around\" 49px -> 55px, byline y 961 -> 968. Stress 21x21 props: title 42px -> 55px, byline y 953 -> 968. Title rect w 541 -> 1002 in every case, including the defaults. The defaults' px only stays the same because 55px is height-capped. The teaser test (test.ts:148-160) checks only labels and texts, not geometry. 30-build.md does not mention it.\n  repro: cd C:/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day && node journal/2026-09-29/review/brief/probe4.cjs\n  fix: Compute the square-mode left column width from p.themes.length > 0 (not solved && themes) so the teaser keeps the solved card's geometry. Add a test that the title/byline/meta rects are the same for solved true and false.\n- low | The meta line is not rendered in the brief's single-spaced format: the first two separators get a 2-4x wider gap\n  evidence: The brief: meta line `<publication> | <Wkd> <M/D/YY> | <cols>x<rows> | solution`, e.g. `Demo Mini | Tue 9/29/26 | 7x7 | solution`. The build draws three cells: \"Demo Mini\", \"| Tue 9/29/26\", \"| 7x7 | solution\". Each cell is placed at leadBoxW(width) = ceil((w+3)/0.94)+1 (ts:482), so the gap before the first two '|' is the box padding, not a space. probe10.cjs at defaults: 1080x1080 px=23, space=5.7px, gaps before the 1st/2nd '|' = 11.7/13.4px (the 3rd '|' uses a normal space). 1920x1080: 13.9/16.5 vs 7.4. 480x270: 7.3/8.1 vs 2.0. It is visible as \"Demo Mini  | Tue 9/29/26  | 7x7 | solution\" in variants/a/stills/square.png, landscape.png and portrait.png. 30-build.md explains the three-cell split but not the uneven spacing.\n  repro: cd C:/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day && node journal/2026-09-29/review/brief/probe10.cjs; look at the caption line in journal/2026-09-29/variants/a/stills/square.png\n  fix: Place each following cell at x + measured ink width + one space width (keep the wider rect for the fit check, or let the rects overlap). Then the three '|' separators get the same spacing.\n- low | 30-build.md says all stress renders had no engine warning, but stress/21x21-480.log records OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP (the 480x270 renders are stale, pre-fix)\n  evidence: 30-build.md: \"Stress renders ... All exit 0, not degraded, with no engine warning: ... plus both grids at 480x270.\" But journal/2026-09-29/stress/21x21-480.log (10:53:05) contains \"[warn] OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP: Mosaic node \\\"root\\\" emits an overlay chain 33 deep (threshold 20) with inline masks riding it\". The 1080 stress renders were redone at 10:54 after the one-source fix, but the 480x270 ones were not. Re-rendering the same props with the current dist (review/brief/21x21-480x270.png) gives no warning. The PNG differs from the stored one in 7388 pixels (board text anti-aliasing), with no visible mask loss. So the current code is fine, but the journal evidence contradicts the build note.\n  repro: cat C:/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day/journal/2026-09-29/stress/21x21-480.log | grep warn; cd C:/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day && m0saic make @one-a-day/gaming/crossword-grid-card/v1 --template-repo . -w 480 -h 270 --props @journal/2026-09-29/stress/21x21.props.json -o journal/2026-09-29/review/brief/21x21-480x270.png\n  fix: Re-render stress/15x15-480x270.png and stress/21x21-480x270.png (and their logs) with the shipped code, or correct the sentence in 30-build.md.\n- low | The contract's `cell` label with an equal-size relation is missing, and the build notes don't say so\n  evidence: The brief's layout contract: \"Label `cell`, relation `equal: \\\"size\\\"` with a tolerance of 0.02 or 1 px ... `latticeCellInset` reports no clamped edges.\" The rendered layoutIntent (probe8.cjs, teaser at 1080) has constraint labels [title, byline-by, byline, meta-publication, meta-date, meta, cell-number, board] and relations undefined. At the defaults the only relation is theme-swatch (ts:726). The code comment at ts:725 says equal cells are left to the test, which asserts lattice-line spread <= 1 (test.ts:188-190). 30-build.md discloses the layer construction but not that debugLayout and the contract no longer check the `cell` relation. The cell-letter/cell-number textFits are measured against the whole-board band rect, not a cell. The test's check uses a 1px slack (budget(hole.w)+1). A full scan (probe5.cjs, 3..25 and non-square sizes at all canvases) found no actual overflow.\n  repro: cd C:/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day && node journal/2026-09-29/review/brief/probe8.cjs\n  fix: State in 30-build.md that equal cells are asserted by the test from the integer lattice, not by a contract `cell` relation (and why: the cells are mask holes, not rects).\n- low | Long theme lists in square mode fall to 8-10 px on the 1080x1080 hint, and to 7 px at 480x270 with 25-letter answers\n  evidence: themeBlock shrinks one shared px down to 6 with no floor (ts:521). The card's own floorPx at 1080 is 14. With the build's stress/21x21 props (8 themes, 21-letter answers), 1080x1080 gives theme-id/theme = 10px, heading 14px (probe2.cjs). The 21x21-1080.png list is barely legible at 1:1 (review/brief/list21-1080-crop.png): the hint canvas gets about the same pixel size as 480x270 (9px). With an open 25x25 and 8 theme answers of 25 letters (probe6.cjs): 1080x1080 -> 8px; 480x270 -> theme-id/theme = 7px, below the brief's \"no panel text is under 8 px at 480x270\". 25-letter answers are outside the brief's 15-21 stress range, but the 8px promise is unqualified and 25x25 is a supported size. 30-build.md only says \"8 long themes in two sub-columns\".\n  repro: cd C:/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day && node journal/2026-09-29/review/brief/probe2.cjs && node journal/2026-09-29/review/brief/probe6.cjs\n  fix: Floor the theme list at floorPx (8px at 480x270). When that doesn't fit, move to 2 sub-columns in landscape and portrait, or disclose the limit. Note in 30-build.md that the 21x21 hint render's list is about 10px.\n- low | At the 4:5 and 5:4 edges of the aspect bands, the portrait board is not full-width, the landscape board is not H-2*margin, and the 1080x1350 header runs into the gutter\n  evidence: The brief: portrait (a <= 0.8) \"sits above a full-width board\"; landscape (a >= 1.25) \"the board is a square of side H - 2*margin\"; gutter \"at least 2x the margin\". At 1080x1350 (a = 0.8, portrait) the board is 670px wide, centred with 205px each side (not full width). The header overflows its band, so the byline sits 73px above the board, below the required 78px (probe7.cjs; review/brief/defaults-1080x1350.png). At 1350x1080 (a = 1.25) the board is 716px, not 1002, and floats with 182px above and below while the title is top-aligned (review/brief/defaults-1350x1080.png). Neither canvas is in CONTRACT_CANVASES, so the sweep doesn't catch it. 4:5 is a common feed canvas.\n  repro: cd C:/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day && node journal/2026-09-29/review/brief/probe7.cjs; view journal/2026-09-29/review/brief/defaults-1080x1350.png and defaults-1350x1080.png\n  fix: Clamp the portrait header to headH (shrink the title/byline) so the gutter holds. Either widen the board budget near the band edges or move the thresholds so 4:5 and 5:4 fall in the square-ish layout. Add 1080x1350 to the geometry test.\nfine: Gutter = 2x margin between board and caption at all seven contract canvases plus the 1080 hint (probe7.cjs: 78/52/156/26/20 px for margins 39/26/78/13/10). || Landscape column is spread: title+byline at top, the theme list centred in the free band, meta at the bottom (variants/a/stills/landscape.png, tutorial-5.png). || Portrait uses the band above the board for title+byline and the band below for the list, with meta at the bottom (portrait.png). The empty band in teaser/no-theme portraits follows from the brief's own \"Nothing else moves\". || Square-mode board side is 0.72 of H (778/1080), centred, with the caption strip below. || Title >= S/20 for the default title at 1080x1080 (55 vs 54), 1920x1080 (81) and 1080x1920 (91). || No panel text under 8 px at 480x270 for every brief stress input, including 21x21 with 8 long themes plus max-length title/author/publication (probe2.cjs). || Size ladder: 15x15 at 1080x1080 gives letters 31px and numbers 14px. Numbers are dropped to 0 below 6px, never shrunk (15x15 at 480x270 -> 0). Letters >= 6px and W fits cell*0.94-2 for every n x n from 3 to 25 and non-square 15x16/3x25/25x3/21x5 at all contract canvases. Rules >= 1px and lattice spread <= 1px (probe5.cjs). || Board >= 0.45 of W and H at the defaults at every contract canvas (0.522/0.928, 0.72). || The THEME ANSWERS heading and list are absent when themeEntries is \"\" or solved is false (showThemes gate; teaser renders). || Meta text is \"Demo Mini | Tue 9/29/26 | 7x7 | solution\", and \"puzzle\" when solved is false. Weekday arithmetic matches Date for 24,472 dates from 1900 to 2100. Feb 29 is validated for leap years, 1900 and 2000. || All rubric-2 validations fail fast with the field named and are tested: ragged row, bad char, lowercase, unknown theme id, duplicate id, circle on a block or out of range, more than 8 themes, bad date, non-hex colour, sizes below 3 and above 25. A 225-char .puz string parses as 15x15. || The teaser document holds no DOGSLED/CATNAPS/grid string/THEME ANSWERS, no cell-letter, theme-tint or theme sources, and its knockouts use paper (probe8.cjs). || Usage page one-liner: `m0saic make ... -w 1080 -h 1080 -o grid.png` writes to a neutral path, and a `solved: false` teaser line is present. || Problem page quotes the Fiend file names, the hand-typed caption and the THEME ANSWERS list. All listed URLs were opened by the scout (Exet was opened by a research agent via fetch-text). || Caveats cover no .puz parser, rebus first letter, shaded squares not drawn, and sizes 3-25. || Ink is legible in greyscale (extra-square-greyscale.png). || npx jest src/gaming/crossword-grid-card: 13/13 pass. || A fresh 21x21 render at 480x270 with the current dist has no OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP warning.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fadc3ba2-c902-457a-8c6b-b57eed4efb97","uuid":"d2d07cf4-6c09-4a38-9032-0b4bd02d77d6","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:13:14.454Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== agent a1b5bc4b982673729\n- medium | At the 1080x1080 hint, a title longer than about 18 characters shrinks below 1/20 of the short side instead of wrapping, and can end up smaller than the byline and theme list\n  evidence: The brief (Panel copy): \"title: the puzzle title, the largest panel text; wraps to at most 2 lines, then shrinks.\" The size ladder: \"The panel title is at least 1/20 of the short side at the primary canvases.\" In square mode the title gets titleMax = panel.h - metaH - bylineH - 2*gap, which is about 67 px (crossword-grid-card.ts:598). That height never fits two lines at a usable size, so fit() shrinks the title on one line. layoutCrosswordCard at 1080x1080 (review/brief/probe3.cjs), against S/20 = 54: \"Turning Things Around\" (21 chars) -> 49px, 1 line; \"A Sunday-Size Stress Grid\" (25) -> 42px; \"Sunday Puzzle: Turning Around\" (29) -> 35px; the 40-char max -> 26px, 1 line. probe12.cjs: with the 40-char title, the title is 26px while byline = 30px and theme-0/theme-1 = 32px, so it is the smallest line in the caption. This is visible in review/brief/max-title-1080.png and titles-strip.png. The build's own rubric-3 render journal/2026-09-29/stress/21x21-1080.png also has a 42px title. The test only checks the 13-c