{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PyJ3atxzaj1qxYM3hmHxSB","type":"tool_result","content":"=== agent a478c16f49213cb62\n- medium | 30-build.md says every stress render had no engine warning, but stress/21x21-480.log has OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP and three stress PNGs are stale pre-fix renders\n  evidence: 30-build.md lines 55-64 say: \"Stress renders ... All exit 0, not degraded, with no engine warning: ... the 15x15 teaser (solved: false), plus both grids at 480x270.\" The log in the same folder disagrees. C:/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day/journal/2026-09-29/stress/21x21-480.log contains: \"[warn] OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP: Mosaic node \\\"root\\\" emits an overlay chain 33 deep (threshold 20) with inline masks riding it. Past ~25 nested overlays ffmpeg SILENTLY degrades inline masks\".\n\nThe build-4.jsonl trace explains why. At #551 (14:52:47Z) all six stress renders ran on the old code, which drew one text source per row. A grep at #593 found three warnings (35, 37 and 33 deep). The fix went in at #645. \n  fix: Re-render stress/15x15-teaser-1080, 15x15-480x270 and 21x21-480x270 (and their .log files) with the current code, then re-read the logs. Otherwise, change the 30-build.md sentence to say those three were rendered before the fix. Replace \"the picture is identical\" with what was actually checked (by e\n- low | Tutorial says the .puz solution string \"pastes as is\", but that only works for square grids\n  evidence: The claim has no conditions in two places. WHY.solution[0] (line 759, rendered on tutorial-3.png) says \"Paste the solution rows from the puzzle file (puzpy's p.solution pastes as is)\". usage.try[0] (line 765, rendered on tutorial-4.png) says \"grid: the .puz solution string\".\n\nparseCrosswordGrid only splits an unbroken string when its length is a perfect square (line 167-170). The brief names 15x16 as a real size. review/truth/puzflat.cjs output:\n- 15x16 (240 chars): \"grid must have 3-25 rows (got 1); split rows with \\\"/\\\" or newlines.\"\n- 16x15 and 21x23: the same error.\n\nWorse, a non-square string whose length happens to be a perfect square is silently mis-read. From review/truth/puzflat2.cj\n  fix: Add a caveat and qualify the usage line, e.g. \"the unbroken .puz string works for square grids; for others, split the rows with /\".\n- low | Usage page never shows how to pass props, so the teaser and grid examples cannot be run from the page\n  evidence: usage.command (line 763) is \"m0saic make @one-a-day/gaming/crossword-grid-card/v1 --template-repo . -w 1080 -h 1080 -o grid.png\", with no --props. It renders only the demo mini (exit 0, pixel-identical to variants/a/renders/square.png). The \"WORTH TRYING\" lines (grid, themeEntries, circles, \"solved: false - the new-puzzle teaser\") give no way to feed them.\n\nThe neighbours' usage pages do: og-card, bench-delta and app-store-screenshot-frame use \"--props @x.json\", and speedrun/powerlifting have a \"--props @props.json with {...}\" try line.\n\nRubric line 4 asks for \"a solved=false teaser example\". The teaser does work: m0saic make ... -w 1080 -h 1080 --props '{\"solved\":false}' -o journal/2026-09-\n  fix: Add a try line such as `--props @puzzle.json with {\"grid\": \"...\", \"themeEntries\": \"17A 38A\", \"solved\": false} - the teaser`, or give a second command for the teaser.\n- low | Problem page cuts the scout's caption quote short without an ellipsis\n  evidence: 10-scout.md line 49-50 records the caption as \"WSJ * 9/22/26 * Tues * \\\"Variety Pack\\\" * Zhoukin Burnikel * solution * 20260922\". The Fiend page text in scout-1.log has the same caption, ending \"solution • 20260922\".\n\nWHY.problem[1] (line 747, rendered on tutorial-2.png) closes the quote after \"solution\" and drops \" * 20260922\", with no ellipsis. The quote reads as the whole caption when it is only a prefix of what the scout recorded.\n  fix: End the quote with \"... solution * 20260922\" or \"... solution ...\".\n- low | 30-build.md says \"Two build calls\" but the runner made four\n  evidence: Line 3 says \"Two build calls. Call 1 (25 min) ... call 4\". logs/runner.log shows four build calls: \"[build] call 1/3 ... exit 1 after 25.4 min\", \"call 2/3 ... exit 1 after 0.0 min\", \"call 3/3 ... exit 1 after 0.0 min\" and \"call 4/6\". logs/build-2.log and build-3.log exist.\n\nOnly two calls did any work, but the count as written is wrong, and the jump from call 1 to call 4 is left unexplained.\n  fix: \"Four build calls: call 1 (25 min) hit the session limit, calls 2 and 3 were refused at once, and call 4 resumed.\"\n- low | Board aspect check in the layout contract fails for very wide grids (25x3) at every canvas\n  evidence: This is outside the truth lens, but it is concrete. I swept every n x n size from 3 to 25, plus 15x16, 3x25, 25x3, 21x23, 13x17 and 25x24, each with and without 8 themes, at 1080x1080 and the 7 contract canvases (464 renders, review/truth/sizes.cjs).\n\nAll of them render, with no overlay depth over 20 and cells equal within 1 px. The one exception is 25x3: checkLayoutIntent fails the \"board\" aspect at all 8 canvases, e.g. \"board aspect 8.146 != 8.333 (+-0.02) [1002x123]\" at 1080x1080 and 7.576 at 480x270.\n\nThe cause is line 722, which declares aspect = cols/rows for the ink rect. That rect includes the border, and the absolute 0.02 tolerance is too tight for large aspects. debugLayout: true w\n  fix: Declare the board aspect from the ink rect's own width and height, or give it a relative tolerance.\n7","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fadc3ba2-c902-457a-8c6b-b57eed4efb97","uuid":"c3587116-7728-4a31-9192-416234b9cda7","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:17:16.480Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== agent a478c16f49213cb62\n- medium | 30-build.md says every stress render had no engine warning, but stress/21x21-480.log has OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP and three stress PNGs are stale pre-fix renders\n  evidence: 30-build.md lines 55-64 say: \"Stress renders ... All exit 0, not degraded, with no engine warning: ... the 15x15 teaser (solved: false), plus both grids at 480x270.\" The log in the same folder disagrees. C:/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day/journal/2026-09-29/stress/21x21-480.log contains: \"[warn] OVERLAY_CHAIN_DEEP: Mosaic node \\\"root\\\" emits an overlay chain 33 deep (threshold 20) with inline masks riding it. Past ~25 nested overlays ffmpeg SILENTLY degrades inline masks\".\n\nThe build-4.jsonl trace explains why. At #551 (14:52:47Z) all six stress renders ran on the old code, which drew one text source per row. A grep at #593 found three warnings (35, 37 and 33 deep). The fix went in at #645. \n  fix: Re-render stress/15x15-teaser-1080, 15x15-480x270 and 21x21-480x270 (and their .log files) with the current code, then re-read the logs. Otherwise, change the 30-build.md sentence to say those three were rendered before the fix. Replace \"the picture is identical\" with what was actually checked (by e\n- low | Tutorial says the .puz solution string \"pastes as is\", but that only works for square grids\n  evidence: The claim has no conditions in two places. WHY.solution[0] (line 759, rendered on tutorial-3.png) says \"Paste the solution rows from the puzzle file (puzpy's p.solution pastes as is)\". usage.try[0] (line 765, rendered on tutorial-4.png) says \"grid: the .puz solution string\".\n\nparseCrosswordGrid only splits an unbroken string when its length is a perfect square (line 167-170). The brief names 15x16 as a real size. review/truth/puzflat.cjs output:\n- 15x16 (240 chars): \"grid must have 3-25 rows (got 1); split rows with \\\"/\\\" or newlines.\"\n- 16x15 and 21x23: the same error.\n\nWorse, a non-square string whose length happens to be a perfect square is silently mis-read. From review/truth/puzflat2.cj\n  fix: Add a caveat and qualify the usage line, e.g. \"the unbroken .puz string works for square grids; for others, split the rows with /\".\n- low | Usage page never shows how to pass props, so the teaser and grid examples cannot be run from the page\n  evidence: usage.command (line 763) is \"m0saic make @one-a-day/gaming/crossword-grid-card/v1 --template-repo . -w 1080 -h 1080 -o grid.png\", with no --props. It renders only the demo mini (exit 0, pixel-identical to variants/a/renders/square.png). The \"WORTH TRYING\" lines (grid, themeEntries, circles, \"solved: false - the new-puzzle teaser\") give no way to feed them.\n\nThe neighbours' usage pages do: og-card, bench-delta and app-store-screenshot-frame use \"--props @x.json\", and speedrun/powerlifting have a \"--props @props.json with {...}\" try line.\n\nRubric line 4 asks for \"a solved=false teaser example\". The teaser does work: m0saic make ... -w 1080 -h 1080 --props '{\"solved\":false}' -o journal/2026-09-\n  fix: Add a try line such as `--props @puzzle.json with {\"grid\": \"...\", \"themeEntries\": \"17A 38A\", \"solved\": false} - the teaser`, or give a second command for the teaser.\n- low | Problem page cuts the scout's caption quote short without an ellipsis\n  evidence: 10-scout.md line 49-50 records the caption as \"WSJ * 9/22/26 * Tues * \\\"Variety Pack\\\" * Zhoukin Burnikel * solution * 20260922\". The Fiend page text in scout-1.log has the same caption, ending \"solution • 20260922\".\n\nWHY.problem[1] (line 747, rendered on tutorial-2.png) closes the quote after \"solution\" and drops \" * 20260922\", with no ellipsis. The quote reads as the whole caption when it is only a prefix of what the scout recorded.\n  fix: End the quote with \"... solution * 20260922\" or \"... solution ...\".\n- low | 30-build.md says \"Two build calls\" but the runner made four\n  evidence: Line 3 says \"Two build calls. Call 1 (25 min) ... call 4\". logs/runner.log shows four build calls: \"[build] call 1/3 ... exit 1 after 25.4 min\", \"call 2/3 ... exit 1 after 0.0 min\", \"call 3/3 ... exit 1 after 0.0 min\" and \"call 4/6\". logs/build-2.log and build-3.log exist.\n\nOnly two calls did any work, but the count as written is wrong, and the jump from call 1 to call 4 is left unexplained.\n  fix: \"Four build calls: call 1 (25 min) hit the session limit, calls 2 and 3 were refused at once, and call 4 resumed.\"\n- low | Board aspect check in the layout contract fails for very wide grids (25x3) at every canvas\n  evidence: This is outside the truth lens, but it is concrete. I swept every n x n size from 3 to 25, plus 15x16, 3x25, 25x3, 21x23, 13x17 and 25x24, each with and without 8 themes, at 1080x1080 and the 7 contract canvases (464 renders, review/truth/sizes.cjs).\n\nAll of them render, with no overlay depth over 20 and cells equal within 1 px. The one exception is 25x3: checkLayoutIntent fails the \"board\" aspect at all 8 canvases, e.g. \"board aspect 8.146 != 8.333 (+-0.02) [1002x123]\" at 1080x1080 and 7.576 at 480x270.\n\nThe cause is line 722, which declares aspect = cols/rows for the ink rect. That rect includes the border, and the absolute 0.02 tolerance is too tight for large aspects. debugLayout: true w\n  fix: Declare the board aspect from the ink rect's own width and height, or give it a relative tolerance.\n7","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-09-29\\logs\\fp-call4.log","hunks":[],"created":true},{"filePath":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\dist\\gaming\\crossword-grid-card\\v1\\crossword-grid-card.js","hunks":[{"oldStart":524,"oldLines":12,"newStart":524,"newLines":15,"lines":["         themeBlock(x, footY + Math.max(0, (free1 - footY - listH) / 2), w, free1 - footY, S * 0.042, 1, false);","     }","     else {","-        const s = boardSizing(cols, rows, W - 2 * margin, H * 0.72);","+        // The column split follows the PROP, not solved: the teaser keeps the solved card's geometry (\"nothing else moves\").","+        const leftW = (W - 2 * margin) * (p.themes.length > 0 ? 0.54 : 1);","+        // A title too long for one line at S/20 wraps to two, and the board gives up that second line's height.","+        const tp = Math.ceil(S / 20);","+        const twoLines = wrap(p.title, tp, (0, text_1.budget)(leftW), true).length > 1;","+        const s = boardSizing(cols, rows, W - 2 * margin, H * 0.72 - (twoLines ? blockH(tp, 2) - blockH(tp, 1) : 0));","         board = boardAt(cols, rows, s, (W - s.inkW) / 2, margin);","         const y0 = board.ink.y + board.ink.h + gutter;","         panel = rect(margin, y0, W - 2 * margin, H - margin - y0);","-        // The column split follows the PROP, not solved: the teaser keeps the solved card's geometry (\"nothing else moves\").","-        const leftW = panel.w * (p.themes.length > 0 ? 0.54 : 1);","         const x = panel.x;","         const mP = metaFit(leftW, panel.h * 0.3, S * 0.022);","         const metaH = mP.height;"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-09-29\\review\\correctness\\t40.props.json","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":1,"lines":["+{\"title\":\"A Title Long Enough To Need Two Lines Ok\"}"]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\dist\\gaming\\crossword-grid-card\\v1\\crossword-grid-card.js","C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-09-29\\logs\\fp-call4.log","C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-09-29\\review\\correctness\\t40.props.json"],"shared":true}}}
