x floor before going under it. Or accept this edge and state that the 8 px floor holds for ordinary text only.\n===== A grid with no entries passes validation but stamps a cell-number constraint on the string '-Infinity' for a label that is never drawn\nEVIDENCE: grid 'A#A/###/A#A' passes parseCrosswordGrid (it has white cells). numbers is empty, so `String(Math.max(...p.numbers.values()))` is \"-Infinity\". Because numberPx > 0, a textFits constraint for 'cell-number' is pushed, but no cell-number source exists (nums is empty). With debugLayout:true the render reports layoutContract ok:false, 'cell-number: missing-label'. This is an implausible grid and the render itself does not crash.\nREPRO: node C:/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day/journal/2026-09-29/review/correctness/06-edge-renders.cjs (first case)\nFIX: Push the cell-number constraint only when nums.length > 0 (p.numbers.size > 0), or refuse a grid with no entries in parseCrosswordGrid with a named message.\n===== The teaser still re-fits the caption line with long copy ('nothing else moves' holds only for the defaults)\nEVIDENCE: With max-length title, author and publication at 1080x1080, going from solved:true to solved:false changes meta-publication from 21 px to 22 px, moves meta-date x from 294 to 306 and moves the tail x from 425 to 443. '| 7x7 | puzzle' is narrower than '| 7x7 | solution', so metaFit lands on a different size. The new 'nothing else moves' test covers only the default props. Title and byline no longer move after the leftW fix.\nREPRO: node C:/src/m0saic-production/one-a-day/journal/2026-09-29/review/correctness/05-teaser-and-cellfit.cjs (the 'max copy @ 1080x1080' block)\nFIX: Fit the meta line on the wider of the two tails (measure with 'solution' in both modes), then draw the actual tail. Extend the test to the max-copy props.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
