n**Fixed after reopening** (each has a test):\n- **Crash on small canvases.** Below about 400 px, a long theme list overflowed the canvas and the engine threw an unnamed error. The list is now dropped when it can't fit even at 6 px; the amber tint on the board still marks the theme entries.\n- **Empty space without a theme.** With `themeEntries: \"\"` (normal for Friday and Saturday puzzles), the landscape column was about 75% empty and the portrait card had a large gap under the board. The landscape title block now centres above the caption line, and portrait spaces the title and caption evenly around the board. A teaser of a themed puzzle keeps the solved card's layout, because the brief says \"nothing else moves\".\n- **Dark theme colour.** A navy `themeColor` hid the letters, numbers and rings. `render()` now refuses a colour below 4.5:1 contrast against the ink and names the field and the ratio. The default is 13.9:1.\n- **Teaser re-fitting the caption.** With long copy the teaser still resized the caption, because \"puzzle\" is narrower than \"solution\". The caption is now always fitted as if it said \"solution\".\n- **Stray constraint.** A grid with no entries added a clue-number layout check for numbers it never draws.\n\n**Checks after the fixes:**\n- `npm run build` is clean and the layout fingerprint is unchanged, since the defaults don't move.\n- `m0saic doctor` reports 0 errors and 0 warnings for this template.\n- `npm test`: 182 jest and 54 pipeline tests pass.\n- Variant a, the stress renders and the new edge-case renders all exit 0 with no engine warnings.\n\n**Still open, all in `30-build.md`:**\n- **Theme list size.** With more than four answers, the square layout splits the list into two sub-columns as the brief asks, and it drops from 19 px to 10–13 px at 1080x1080. That is smaller than its own heading.\n- **Byline floor.** A 48-character author of wide letters (48 × \"W\") goes to 7 px at 480x270, under the 8 px promise. Real names stay at 8 px